WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:09.279
In this video, we'll get a
laptop ready for the workshop.

2
00:00:09.279 --> 00:00:13.055
First, redeem your free
month of GitHub Copilot

3
00:00:13.055 --> 00:00:17.151
Max at github.com/redeem,
with the workshop's code.

4
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:22.943
You add a payment method, and it renews
on its own, so set a reminder to cancel.

5
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:29.611
Then open the Agents window in
VS Code Insiders, signed in with GitHub.

6
00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:32.282
Open your user settings as JSON.

7
00:00:32.712 --> 00:00:37.433
Add a comma after the last line, and paste
the 16 workshop settings from the site.

8
00:00:38.548 --> 00:00:42.630
They turn on what we use
tonight, like Computer Use,

9
00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:47.732
canvases and automations,
and they turn the terminal sandbox off.

10
00:00:47.939 --> 00:00:53.765
Save, then quit and reopen
VS Code Insiders, so they take effect.

11
00:00:55.033 --> 00:00:58.040
Here's the composer,
where every session starts.

12
00:00:58.367 --> 00:01:01.895
Where it runs. This Computer
means your own laptop.

13
00:01:02.084 --> 00:01:05.603
The workspace. For setup,
we chat without a folder.

14
00:01:06.917 --> 00:01:09.706
The agent that runs it. We use Copilot.

15
00:01:11.922 --> 00:01:17.101
More options, the prompt,
and Add Context for files and screenshots.

16
00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:24.570
Then mode and permissions,
the model, dictation, and Send.

17
00:01:28.981 --> 00:01:33.265
For the workshop, keep the mode on
Interactive, and set permissions

18
00:01:33.265 --> 00:01:37.422
to Allow all, so the agent doesn't
stop to ask before every step.

19
00:01:42.045 --> 00:01:46.439
The settings already turned
Sandboxing for terminal off.

20
00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:54.324
Pick GPT-6.2 Sol, and set the effort to High.

21
00:01:56.629 --> 00:01:59.567
The context size is how much
the model can keep in mind.

22
00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:03.355
Prices are in credits per million tokens.

23
00:02:03.355 --> 00:02:07.489
One credit is one cent,
and Copilot Max comes with 20,000 a month.

24
00:02:08.332 --> 00:02:11.960
There are models from several
companies, each with its own price.

25
00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:15.007
You can also add your own key from a provider

26
00:02:15.007 --> 00:02:17.851
like OpenRouter, or sign
in with a ChatGPT plan.

27
00:02:18.192 --> 00:02:21.376
Now paste the setup prompt
from the site, and send it.

28
00:02:26.334 --> 00:02:29.131
This is a real run, with the waits sped up.

29
00:02:29.131 --> 00:02:33.359
The agent reads the setup guide
and downloads the workshop files.

30
00:02:35.375 --> 00:02:37.997
The setup canvas opens right in the chat.

31
00:02:38.277 --> 00:02:42.530
Pick AI-First Design, the workshop
for designers on their own laptops.

32
00:02:45.745 --> 00:02:49.505
It tells you what's about to happen.
Nothing installs until you confirm.

33
00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:54.863
Here's what it installs, with sizes.

34
00:02:54.863 --> 00:02:59.032
The essentials are locked on,
and the extras are up to you.

35
00:03:02.439 --> 00:03:05.821
About 195 megabytes in all.

36
00:03:06.395 --> 00:03:10.374
And how to undo it all later,
with a guide and a video.

37
00:03:12.461 --> 00:03:16.138
After Confirm, the agent installs
what you checked, makes your

38
00:03:16.138 --> 00:03:19.876
own copy of Excalidraw on GitHub,
and tells you when it's done.

39
00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.321
Each item turns green when it's set up.

40
00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:33.405
Before it makes your public practice
repo and its live site, it asks. Say yes.

41
00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:40.723
Now it makes your copy of the case
study on GitHub, turns on its live

42
00:03:40.723 --> 00:03:44.606
site, clones it into the workshop
folder and installs what it needs.

43
00:03:47.117 --> 00:03:50.186
Done. Everything you checked is set up.

44
00:03:54.917 --> 00:03:58.306
To finish, try dictation and Computer Use.

45
00:03:58.306 --> 00:04:03.631
Copy the Try it prompt from the
canvas into the chat, and send it.
